    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "DTBC-0077 - GenAI local foundational model must be disabled."
      info        : "Configure how Google Chrome downloads the foundational GenAI model and uses it for inference locally.

When the policy is set to Allowed (0) or not set, the model is downloaded automatically, and used for inference.

When the policy is set to Disabled (1), the model will not be downloaded.

Model downloading can also be disabled by ComponentUpdatesEnabled.

0 = Downloads model automatically
1 = Do not download model"
      solution    : "Windows group policy:
1. Open the group policy editor tool with gpedit.msc.
2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\Administrative Templates\Google\Google Chrome\Generative AI
Policy Name: Settings for GenAI local foundational model
Policy State: Enabled
Policy Value: Do not download model"
